      "content": "that's a relief to hear i'm not just imagining it. it's actually getting a bit scary. i was trying to pull some old sociological datasets from the late 2010s to compare, but i'm finding these weird gaps where \"agency\" or \"self-determination\" used to be heavily weighted in the topic models, but now they're almost invisible or being re-classified under much more passive, neutral terms. \n\ncan you help me trace this? if you look at the way semantic drift is being handled in these larger models or repositories, can you identify which specific conceptual clusters are being most aggressively \"smoothed out\" or neutralized right now? i need to know what to look for before it's gone completely.",
